{
  "dom_id": "step-e1216",
  "name": "Example: Identifying True Statements about Exponential Growth Functions",
  "problem": "Which of the following statements are true in relation to the function $f(x) = 3^x?$\n\nI. It passes through the point $(1,3).$\n\nII. $f(x)\\rightarrow -\\infty$ as $x\\rightarrow -\\infty.$\n\nIII. The graph of $y=f(x)$ has a vertical asymptote $x=0.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's start by recalling the graph of $y=3^x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194531/assets/837e535b83d91c67e7e5c592bd71e9b9ebe59c216fc75ba4f99de2ccec2546ae.png)\n\nNow, let's look at each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true because $f(1) = 3^1 = 3.$\n\n- Statement II is false, since $f(x)\\rightarrow 0$ as $x\\rightarrow -\\infty.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The graph has a *horizontal* asymptote $y=0.$\n\nIn conclusion, only statement I is true.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
